{
  "task": "G6-067",
  "status": "G6-067 complete for approved implementation and local fixture scope; independent acceptance remains unqualified",
  "checked_at": "2026-10-26T17:30:24.806741+00:00",
  "base_revision": "e9a7186d331ab48108006a3cc8c48719697123cf",
  "scope": "Local Darwin arm64 storage-independent v2 contract/API, Vapi/Telnyx/SIP mappings, independent actual in-process PCMU adapter, owned canonical Core installation/failure recovery and current CLI/HTTP. No real account/model-host, process-crash durability, network/browser/Linux/remote/profile/latency/capacity, installed package, full stock application journey, publication or acceptance claim.",
  "implementation": [
    "Replace manifest v1 audio/video fields with a strict v2 union: unsupported, PCM lifecycle fixture or live binding. No version-1 fallback or implicit media capability. Retain normalized message/voice observations, configuration references, immutable registration and protected host responsibilities.",
    "Describe direct rvoip Transport adapters separately from enrolled signed native Endpoint hosts. Bound unique codec-family catalogs; negotiated-only media refuses static readiness claims. Explicit liveness, inbound handoff, terminal fallback, staged origination and replacement guarantees constrain runtime binding. Context and recording remain current host policies.",
    "Trusted server composition derives runtime facts from the existing real ConnectionAdapter interface without provider-name branches. Canonical SIP startup validates its supplied adapter and records its immutable declaration; canonical Vapi native startup records a separate PCMU/native/context profile after existing Endpoint/key/source checks. Telephone API and SMS stay media-unsupported.",
    "Migrate both standalone lifecycle fixtures and the API-only export/checker to v2. A fixture exchange cannot satisfy a live runtime claim. New contract tests cover runtime/binding mismatch, codec refusal, negotiated-only readiness, restart policy drift and closed fields.",
    "Add the independently buildable public-interface media fixture: bounded actual PCMU source and decoder, staged host effect custody, original full-intent replay, generation guards, explicit unsupported inbound/media controls, atomic Core lifecycle queue and terminal cancellation/drain ownership. No Connect Store/service dependency.",
    "LiveMediaLifecycle is a storage-independent cancellation/drain contract. LiveTransport binds it to the exact same typed rvoip adapter Arc, validates configuration references and immutable runtime declarations, rejects duplicate names/transports and installs on the actual canonical Core before intake. No provider-name branch or principal/Endpoint/Conversation grant is introduced.",
    "CanonicalConnectors composes optional message/SMS policy and contributed live transports. Startup refusal observes bounded concurrent drains; cancellation/Drop synchronously request permanent admission fencing. Shutdown reports cleanup deadlines/failure as unconfirmed. Large startup futures are heap-owned to keep the default runtime/test stack bounded."
  ],
